    "summary": "Single-stage spur gear reducer, 3:1. A pinion on the input shaft meshes with a wheel on the output shaft. Both gears are keyed and seated against shaft shoulders. Each shaft runs in two deep-groove ball bearings in a split housing (base and cover) with bolted bearing caps.",
    "assumptions": [
      "The 3:1 ratio is a single spur pinion/wheel pair. Module, teeth and widths are left for standard sizing.",
      "Each shaft leaves the housing on one side only. That side gets an open cap and the opposite side a blind cap.",
      "The input and output shafts may need different bearing sizes, so each shaft has its own bearing entry.",
      "Each gear is keyed and sits against a shoulder on a stepped shaft.",
      "There are no seals, couplings or shaft-end keys, because the brief does not ask for them.",
      "Fastener counts are typical: 4 screws per cap and 6 bolts joining the cover to the base."
